                    {
                        "form_id": "4a0e47b9-f73e-4f28-bef2-02218028605a",
                        "entry_id": "50e60433-41f5-30f7-97bb-04406dbd9b00",
                        "tags": [
                            "diminutive",
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "dwingelandjes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fe9fd349-767a-3bfa-a016-8cd002618237",
                        "entry_id": "50e60433-41f5-30f7-97bb-04406dbd9b00",
                        "glosses": [
                            "iemand die op een hinderlijke manier de baas speelt of probeert te spelen"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6d580242-0c21-4ad6-ba7a-93fde1bbea7c",
                                "sense_id": "fe9fd349-767a-3bfa-a016-8cd002618237",
                                "text": "Gezien dit hooggestemde ideaal en zijn diepe afkeer van sociale conventies, die hij als onecht en hypocriet ontmaskert, zou je hem een romanticus kunnen noemen, maar dan een van de norse soort. Als hij voor een scheerbeurt naar de kapper gaat, legt hij een bedrag neer en zegt: ‘Dit is voor jou als je je mond houdt tot je klaar bent met scheren. Als je praat neem ik het weer mee.’ Inderdaad, onconventioneel. Aangezien hij zich verder in de relaties die hij aanknoopt als een dwingeland en eersteklas manipulator ontpopt, is C. geen personage om in je hart te sluiten. Daar staat tegenover dat hij als weerbarstig, moeilijk te peilen sujet de lezer wel uitdaagt en intrigeert."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "920a51a2-4af6-480d-95b5-da7a3c5f2bb2",
                                "sense_id": "fe9fd349-767a-3bfa-a016-8cd002618237",
                                "text": "In het Noord-Brabantse Reusel heerst een godsdiensttwist die het dorp splijt. De bron van de onvrede: de pastoor. Een orthodoxe dwingeland, zeggen parochianen. In een stille tocht eisen ze zijn vertrek. 'We hebben moeder maar laten cremeren.'"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4c8d7b44-c274-4334-81df-804a05d3531b",
                        "source_entry_id": "50e60433-41f5-30f7-97bb-04406dbd9b00",
                        "source_sense_id": "fe9fd349-767a-3bfa-a016-8cd002618237",
                        "source_sense_description": "iemand die op een hinderlijke manier de baas probeert te spelen",
                        "target_lang_word": "tyrant",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "tyrant",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ec430fd6-234d-3c6f-b197-7299929b300a",
                                        "entry_id": "b599476b-75d7-3f8e-bc1a-693b48833340",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A usurper; one who gains power and rules extralegally, distinguished from kings elevated by election or succession."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "86a86ebd-355a-4d13-a72a-7146e5d0c2c5",
                                                "sense_id": "ec430fd6-234d-3c6f-b197-7299929b300a",
                                                "text": "To proue him Tyrant, this reason may suffice, That Henry liueth still."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f2ac3046-b7cc-49c8-918a-20239500ac0d",
                                                "sense_id": "ec430fd6-234d-3c6f-b197-7299929b300a",
                                                "text": "The reappearance of tyranny [in the 4th century BC] had many reasons... one of the main causes was the development of antagonism between rich and poor; tyrants came to power exploiting a social and political imbalance within the state."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1c5a437e-d254-44ba-86c3-31402795adad",
                                                "sense_id": "ec430fd6-234d-3c6f-b197-7299929b300a",
                                                "text": "Ancient Greek tyrannies appeared once more in great numbers with the breakdown of the polis in the period from the fourth to the second centuries [BC]. These later tyrannies tended to rely on a more narrow class base and to use a brutal military rule, and thus writers could use the words tyrant and tyranny, with their modern connotations of evil and cruelty, to describe them accurately."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "925d4ba9-60d3-35a6-a37c-a248d0a9ad7a",
                                        "entry_id": "b599476b-75d7-3f8e-bc1a-693b48833340",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any monarch or governor."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2df5f185-6248-444c-bed2-acf073bf9acf",
                                                "sense_id": "925d4ba9-60d3-35a6-a37c-a248d0a9ad7a",
                                                "text": "Cassius... set tyrants over all Syria."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a05f3c66-84fd-3892-9f0b-25e8eaed1fa4",
                                        "entry_id": "b599476b-75d7-3f8e-bc1a-693b48833340",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A despot; a ruler who governs unjustly, cruelly, or harshly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5cee4cab-ed90-4663-9249-38931031b545",
                                                "sense_id": "a05f3c66-84fd-3892-9f0b-25e8eaed1fa4",
                                                "text": "Tyrannes...be but Gods scourges which he will cast into the fyre when he hath done with them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "54e6460b-3691-46d6-977b-9d912f54d773",
                                                "sense_id": "a05f3c66-84fd-3892-9f0b-25e8eaed1fa4",
                                                "text": "I am the Sonne of Marcus Cato, hoe.\nA Foe to Tyrants, and my Countries Friend."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2abdcbfa-e969-4a33-8c76-f1873babc7bc",
                                                "sense_id": "a05f3c66-84fd-3892-9f0b-25e8eaed1fa4",
                                                "text": "Here is a Proclamation for a Prince: that proclaims him in whoſe name it is emitted [James II of England], to be the greateſt Tyrant that ever lived in the world, and their Revolt who have diſowned him to be the juſteſt that ever was."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "07c031ee-8f80-4c3d-86ca-815a4944e946",
                                                "sense_id": "a05f3c66-84fd-3892-9f0b-25e8eaed1fa4",
                                                "text": "They [viz., the Framers of the American Constitution] held England to be the freest and best-governed country in the world, but were resolved to avoid the weak points which had enabled King George III. to play the tyrant, and which rendered English liberty, as they thought, far inferior to that which the constitutions of their own States secured."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "14df0dbe-98a7-3d74-9601-bd307727d9fa",
                                        "entry_id": "b599476b-75d7-3f8e-bc1a-693b48833340",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any person who abuses the power of position or office to treat others unjustly, cruelly, or harshly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3a32c6c7-0050-407d-bf90-e558571cd42d",
                                                "sense_id": "14df0dbe-98a7-3d74-9601-bd307727d9fa",
                                                "text": "A plague vpon the Tyrant that I serue"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "544506b6-0081-4457-b35a-415c26b6d51e",
                                                "sense_id": "14df0dbe-98a7-3d74-9601-bd307727d9fa",
                                                "text": "[…] a sad tyrant, as my friends the Democrats sometimes are."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "05bbe2cb-0a79-3486-8ce2-3e10e20c1689",
                                        "entry_id": "b599476b-75d7-3f8e-bc1a-693b48833340",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A villain; a person or thing who uses strength or violence to treat others unjustly, cruelly, or harshly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0faeced5-32cc-460b-90a4-81bfb57f11d4",
                                                "sense_id": "05bbe2cb-0a79-3486-8ce2-3e10e20c1689",
                                                "text": "I was a blasphemar, and a persecuter, and a tyraunt."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bb2a7537-3b6a-4d13-866f-2a7f76b4264a",
                                                "sense_id": "05bbe2cb-0a79-3486-8ce2-3e10e20c1689",
                                                "text": "A pike (called the tyranne of fishes)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f4a122b8-7783-4911-8c85-1af60e3aa53c",
                                                "sense_id": "05bbe2cb-0a79-3486-8ce2-3e10e20c1689",
                                                "text": "O dissembling Curtesie! How fine this Tyrant Can tickle where she wounds?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "876331f7-2bd3-4fcc-ae04-df2d8e87662d",
                                                "sense_id": "05bbe2cb-0a79-3486-8ce2-3e10e20c1689",
                                                "text": "Public opinion, the greatest tyrant of these times."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fa289a47-65d4-3d35-b76c-61e8f0da0d25",
                                        "entry_id": "b599476b-75d7-3f8e-bc1a-693b48833340",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The tyrant birds, members of the family Tyrannidae, which often fight or drive off other birds which approach their nests."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1260d2b6-04c7-40b2-ae3e-b057ffb28654",
                                                "sense_id": "fa289a47-65d4-3d35-b76c-61e8f0da0d25",
                                                "text": "Tyrant or Tyrant-bird, Catesby applied it solely to...the King-bird..., but apparently as much in reference to its bright crown...as to its tyrannical behaviour to other birds."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b92872cd-964d-4688-88da-a743f985c61a",
                                                "sense_id": "fa289a47-65d4-3d35-b76c-61e8f0da0d25",
                                                "text": "The Tyrant... The courage of this little Bird is singular."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1553db7e-ec9c-499c-977b-3036347d16dd",
                                                "sense_id": "fa289a47-65d4-3d35-b76c-61e8f0da0d25",
                                                "text": "The lesser tyrants (Tyrannulae) are spread over the whole of America, where they represent the true flycatcher... The tyrants are bold and quarrelsome birds, particularly during the season of incubation."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "tyrant",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a36cac05-6c39-322d-9f81-1a7d368d22ee",
                                        "entry_id": "f2ea527d-1942-35bb-9843-1cb3a0eb310f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Tyrannical, tyrannous; like, characteristic of, or in the manner of a tyrant."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncommon"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7ff6c886-f73a-42b9-af51-d0af0fb10b11",
                                                "sense_id": "a36cac05-6c39-322d-9f81-1a7d368d22ee",
                                                "text": "He was most tirant & cruell of all emperours."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dccc9831-ecfb-40a0-95f3-9bee805ecb32",
                                                "sense_id": "a36cac05-6c39-322d-9f81-1a7d368d22ee",
                                                "text": "Thus must I from the smoake into the smother,\nFrom tyrant Duke, vnto a tyrant Brother."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "98b27ad3-c013-4e92-9a13-86c986721f33",
                                                "sense_id": "a36cac05-6c39-322d-9f81-1a7d368d22ee",
                                                "text": "...a reconciliation between our no longer parent state, but tyrant state, and these colonies."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "tyrant",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "15f116c2-93ef-3156-98ec-12699abf776f",
                                        "entry_id": "1de80be5-ba4c-3f3f-ad0f-9a9bbb448efe",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To act like a tyrant; to be tyrannical."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e424ddaa-fe4f-4659-8c0a-07025c2e7ec1",
                                                "sense_id": "15f116c2-93ef-3156-98ec-12699abf776f",
                                                "text": "Let thy judgment be king, but not tyrant over it"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "99f77dbd-03b7-3886-88a9-51b7e17c1853",
                                        "entry_id": "1de80be5-ba4c-3f3f-ad0f-9a9bbb448efe",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To tyrannize."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
